ED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm indurated gray pink tumor mass at approximately the 12 o clock position which comes to  0 1cm from the anterior margin and 0 2cm from the posterior margin  Located 3 0cm inferior and lateral to the mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 3cm area of dense gray white fibrous tissue with indurated tan pink tumor masses throughout ranging from REMOVED_DATE to roughly 3 5cm in greatest dimension  The tumor masses occupy approximately 80  of this dense fibrous region  This area comes to 0 2cm of the posterior margin  Adjacent to this region along the medial aspect is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm tan yellow serous fluid filled cyst with a smooth  glistening gray white fibrous lining measuring 0 1cm in thickness  The cyst wall comes to 0 3cm of the posterior margin  Located 2 0cm superior to the cyst  3 0cm medial to the dense gray white fibrous mass and 1 5cm inferomedial to the first mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm indurated gray pink nodule which comes to 0 4cm of the posterior margin  Sectioning of the axillary region reveals several tan red possible lymph nodes averaging 0 4cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Largest tumor mass submitted from lateral to medial with posterior margins in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Well defined tumor mass to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cyst to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial most  smallest tumor mass to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple possible lymph nodes  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm aggregate of tan pink fibroadipose tissue which is sectioned to reveal multiple tan red lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 2 1cm in greatest dimension  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as 