shows focal yellow orange areas consistent with fat necrosis  The cavity comes to 1 7cm of the posterior margin  and a silver metal clip is noted within the wall of the cavity along the anterior lateral aspect  The surrounding gray pink fibrous tissue is diffusely nodular with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  Sectioning of the designated axillary region reveals a few possible tan pink lymph nodes  averaging 0 2cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity closest to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Anterior lateral cavity at silver metal clip   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Inferior cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial uninvolved tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral uninvolved tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Possible lymph nodes  in toto   Gross Dictation by Stephanie Kuehn  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Melinda J Lerwill M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , 0.
