Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 07 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  SEE NOTE   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  ADJACENT TO THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SKIN WITH DERMAL NEVUS  NOTE  All margins are free of carcinoma  No blood vessel or lymphatic vessel invasion is identified  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TWELVE OF TWELVE LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Jacqueline Haas  MD Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 14                                                                                     BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY ADDENDUM Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 24 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast and axillary contents   is a 28 x 17 x REMOVED_DATE right modified radical mastectomy specimen with an overlying 17 x 5 5cm skin ellipse with a centrally placed grossly unremarkable nipple with no scar identified  The breast is inked  serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm well circumscribed firm white mass  grossly coming to within 2 0cm of the closest deep inked margin  and 2 2cm from the overlying skin ellipse  The mass is surrounded by nodular firm fibrous tissue with areas of hemorrhage  The remainde